# What this node ships is the node; what it generates is never anyone's history.
#
# A group's content is two files — `IDEAS.md` (the sign) and `graph.json` (the last
# published version). Everything a group generates besides those two is named here once,
# at any depth, so a group living anywhere under this node is safe by default:
#   `.graph.json`  live state, rewritten on every gesture
#   `ops.jsonl`    the account, one line per change
#   `.versions/`   a snapshot per save — regenerable, and it grows without a bound
#   `.trash/`      what an import moved aside
#   `.lock`        this process's hold on the group
#   `runtime/`     node process logs (stdout/stderr per launch)
**/.graph.json
**/ops.jsonl
**/.versions/
**/.trash/
**/.lock
/runtime/
__pycache__/

# A group is unpublished by default: nothing under the data root enters git unless it is
# named here once. A published group's own .gitignore then decides what inside it ships
# (the sign, the published graph.json) and what stays out.
/ideas/*
!/ideas/mosshell-stage3-todos/
